**Agent registry rule:** edit agent/skill/command definitions only under
`agents/` — never in `~/.claude/*` or tool config dirs (those are symlinks
or synced copies). After editing, run `./scripts/sync-agents.sh`.

## 3. Authority map — where truth actually lives

This vault contains **copies**. Before answering questions about code,
consult the authoritative source, not a snapshot:

| Topic | Authoritative source |
|---|---|
| Protocol/code design, build, test | `/root/kovanica-protocol` — read its `AGENTS.md` first |
| Deployed testnet ops | `KovanicaDAG/TESTNET.md`, `OPERATIONS.md`, `kovanica-node/` (snapshot; verify against kovanica-protocol) |
| Project overview as presented in Obsidian | `KovanicaDAG/myObsidianVaultDAG.md` |

When the code changes and you are asked to update docs: pull facts from
`/root/kovanica-protocol` (source, module docs, its
roadmap), then update the relevant snapshot here.

## 4. Recipe — update notes & push ("vault sync")

1. Make the requested edits under `KovanicaDAG/`.
2. `git add -A && git commit -m "docs: <what changed>"`
3. If push rejected: `git pull --rebase origin main`, resolve if needed.
4. `git push origin main`

Commit subjects: imperative, prefixed `docs:` (e.g. `docs: sync vault
snapshot (project config files)`).

## 5. Never commit / never touch as git content

- `.obsidian/`, `.claudian/`, `.trash/` — ignored (app state, session data).
- `KovanicaDAG/KovanicaDAG/` — **embedded stale copies of the real project
  repos** (they contain their own `.git`). Ignored on purpose; committing
  them creates broken phantom submodules. Do not un-ignore, do not clean up
  without asking.
- Never convert the `kovanica-*` doc folders into submodules — history shows
  submodule attempts failed and were deliberately removed.

## 6. Working notes for assistants

- **Do not invent** APIs, paths, commands, or roadmap items. If a fact isn't
  verifiable in kovanica-protocol or these docs, say so.
- Snapshots under `KovanicaDAG/` (and `kovanica-node/`) are refreshed by
  `scripts/sync-vault.sh` from `/root/kovanica-protocol`; `myObsidianVaultDAG.md`
  is the vault-specific overview. Prefer `myObsidianVaultDAG.md` and the
  protocol repo itself when snapshots disagree with reality.
- Verify before claiming: run commands, don't assume output.
